# Line endings are part of a type's IDENTITY here, so they are not left to each
# machine's git settings.
#
# A letter names its program by the sha256 of its bytes, and the built-in types
# are samples/*.html embedded at build time. With no rule, a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true -- the default there, and on GitHub's Windows runners)
# turns every LF into CRLF: the app still works, but its "Memo" is a different
# type from the Memo built on Linux or macOS, under a different hash. The
# welcome forum's roster was very nearly published as an instance of a Group
# type that exists only in CRLF builds.
#
# So: every text file is LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Signed bundles and images are bytes. Never let git "fix" them.
*.thing binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
